  "method": "Actual frozen LibraryManager.GetPerson/GetPersonId/GetGenreId/GetMusicGenreId/GetStudioId, DtoService.AttachPeople/AttachBasicFields/AttachGenreItems/AttachStudios, Person.IsVisible, ImageProcessor.GetImageCacheTag and JsonDefaults serialization. People attachment precedes basic fields, matching the native production order. Each people case also executes PeopleRepository.UpdatePeople through its actual CLR Name/Role normalization, stopping with an explicit sentinel from the first CreateDbContext call. Both actual PeopleRepository.Map overloads then convert normalized PersonInfo to People entities and People/PeopleBaseItemMap back to PersonInfo before a second native DTO projection. Raw outputs are retained as People; mapped outputs are persistedPeople. Original 30-case output remains byte-for-byte in native-raw.json.",
  "isolation": "Synthetic in-memory BaseItem repository and interface stubs. No reference database, actual media, image bytes or user state are read or written. Native reference source is read only for hash comparison.",
  "limits": [
    "Private methods are called by reflection, not through full HTTP.",
    "Repository rows and collection folders are stubbed.",
    "UpdatePeople stops before opening a database. This adds actual normalization and mapper coverage, not EF transactions or database writes. Case-insensitive credit de-duplication and ListOrder assignment follow the source before invoking actual mapper overloads.",
    "Permission cases cover tags, missing people and by-name exemptions; textual parental rating/country recomputation is not covered.",
    "Image tests exercise stored descriptors, blurhash aggregation and native cache tags; no image decoding or downloading.",
    "Other DTO fields and native database persistence are outside these samples."
  ],
